== C7 No float artifacts anywhere a user sees or hears: FAIL
D1 — formatExact (render.go:616, `math.Round(v*1e10) / 1e10`) does not compute "the shortest decimal of the value rounded to 10 places" for real cent values. It prints binary-float noise into visible number fields.
- Repro in a real server (fixture A with taxable_cost_basis 388354.59, S/fxK):
  - `curl /whatif`: id="taxable-cost-basis-input" value="388354.5900000001".
  - Hidden portfolio_value (fixture 262144.03): value="262144.0300000001".
  - Chromium (S/js/artifact.js): the Cost Basis input's .value is "388354.5900000001". Screenshot S/costbasis.brK.png shows that text in the field.
  - Firing the form's own change trigger (untouched) POSTed "taxable_cost_basis=388354.5900000001" and "portfolio_value=262144.0300000001". Saved JSON is now 388354.5900000001 / 262144.0300000001 (basisBitEqual false).
- Lead's own oracle: a scratch copy of .swarm/tier3/WS1 with only the fixture's cost basis changed 276146.86 -> 388354.59 (S/oraclecopy), run against the snapshot, gives:
  - "FAIL E2 (D4): no float artifacts shown or announced (['taxable_cost_basis=388354.5900000001'])".
  - Last line "ORACLE FAIL". Criterion 1 still PASSes there, within 1e-9.
- Mechanism: 388354.59*1e10 is 3883545900000000.5 in float64. math.Round rounds half away from zero to ...001, and /1e10 then lands 1 ulp above the stored value. For |v| >= 1e8 the product is not exact at all.
- Extent (temporary Go test calling the real formatExact, S/probes/):
  - Exhaustive by cent over $0-$100,000: 0 of 10,000,000 values affected.
  - $100,000-$900,000: 1,505,728 of 80,000,000 (1.9%), the smallest being $262,144.03.
  - Sampled $900K-$100M: 0 of 3,000,000 samples.
  - Sampled $100M-$1B: 40,683 of 500,000 (8.1%).
  - Whole dollars 0-20M, 3- and 4-decimal percents 0-100, and COLA x100 (0-0.1 by 0.0001): 0 artifacts.
  - Exposed fields, all rendered with formatExact:
    - taxable_cost_basis: visible, max 1e9.
    - roth annual_amount: visible, max 1e6.
    - portfolio_value: hidden, but the stored value is rewritten.
  - The oracle fixture (276146.86) and the Go fixtures are not affected values, so both pass.
- Attempt-1 D4 values are now clean (`curl`): COLA 0.028->"2.8", 0.029->"2.9", 0.059->"5.9", 0.07->"7", 0.0145->"1.45". Oracle "PASS E2" on its own fixture.
- Missing: a formatExact whose output is the shortest decimal of the value correctly rounded to 10 places, for every magnitude a WS1 field can hold (at least up to 1e9), plus a test that pins it (e.g. 388354.59, 262144.03, 255122409.87).

